![Architecture](../diagrams/architecture.png)

## Prerequisites
- AWS account (dedicated lab account recommended)
- Terraform ~> 1.9
- AWS CLI v2 configured with a profile named `hipaa-labs`
- ~$X estimated cost if left running 24h (we'll calculate this for real)

## Deploy
```bash
cd terraform
cp terraform.tfvars.example terraform.tfvars
# edit terraform.tfvars
terraform init
terraform plan -out=tfplan
terraform apply tfplan
```

## Verify
```bash
cd ../verification
./verify.sh
```
[Then link to athena-queries.md for the audit trail queries]

## Tear down
```bash
cd terraform
terraform destroy
```
[Note about CloudTrail log bucket — versioning + retention. Manual
cleanup may be required if you've enabled MFA delete. Be explicit.]

## Cost
[Real numbers. KMS key = $1/month + $0.03 per 10k requests. CloudTrail
management events free, data events $0.10 per 100k. S3 standard pricing.
Estimate for 24h running idle vs the verify run.]

## What I'd do differently in production
[3–5 bullets. Honest. Things deliberately simplified for the lab —
remote state, multi-region trail, KMS multi-region keys, separate
log archive account, Config rules for compliance drift detection.
This section is what separates a portfolio lab from a tutorial.]

